DiscoBSD/GBA native ARM toolchain - development prototypes (Phase 1b + 1c).
Full status in sys/arch/gba/NOTES.toolchain sections 8-9.

These are HOST development prototypes that prove the design end to end. They
are validated but NOT yet folded into usr.bin/as / usr.bin/ld or the build.

asarm.c  - ARM (ARMv4T) assembler for the exact subset usr.bin/smlrc/cgarm.c
           emits. Two modes:
             asarm -e "<one instr>"  -> print the 32-bit encoding (oracle)
             asarm in.s out.bin      -> flat text+data image (labels + literal
                                        pools resolved)
             asarm -c in.s out.o     -> DiscoBSD a.out RELOCATABLE OBJECT
                                        (header/segments/symtab/ARM relocs)
           Validated: 42/42 encodings byte-exact vs arm-none-eabi-as; 22/22
           single-object programs run in Unicorn.

ldarm.c  - ARM linker. Reads asarm's a.out objects, lays out text/data/bss,
           resolves globals, applies ARM relocs (ABS32 + PC24), writes a flat
           linked image + prints ENTRY/SYM.
             ldarm -Ttext=<hex> -e <entry> -o out.bin a.o b.o ...
           (Thumb interworking veneers: not needed while all-ARM; TODO for a
           Thumb libc.)

FULL SELF-HOSTED CHAIN (no GNU tools): smlrc-arm -> asarm -c -> ldarm -> run.
Validated on cross-object calls, bss globals, division via a self-hosted
__aeabi runtime (rt.c), recursion, loops, arrays.

Build + validate (needs arm-none-eabi-as only for the encoder oracle; Unicorn
for execution):
  pip install --user --break-system-packages unicorn
  # smlrc-arm: see NOTES.toolchain section 7 for the exact gcc -DARM line
  gcc -O1 -o asarm asarm.c
  gcc -O1 -o ldarm ldarm.c
  python3 run_ld.py        # or run.py / run_asarm.py

Test inputs: suite.c exta.c big.c lib.c app.c divp.c rt.c
Harnesses:   run.py (via arm-none-eabi-ld+libgcc), run_asarm.py (asarm flat),
             run_ld.py (asarm -c + ldarm, fully self-hosted)
